smartclockmon (0.6.8-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Plot the satellite count.  It was recorded and not plottable, which
    made "is it tracking?" a database question rather than a glance.
  * Counts get an axis pinned to their range, starting at zero and
    stepping in whole numbers, so a count that never left zero no longer
    draws an axis from -1 to 1.
  * Sixteen commands, then nine more, added to the Z3801 dialect --
    temperature, oven current, EFC count, TFOM, date, time and the
    position group -- confirmed against a Z3805A.
  * Say the oscillator temperature coefficient's units rather than
    calling them undocumented: parts in 10^12 per degree C.
  * Test databases delete their write-ahead files, which had been
    accumulating in the temporary directory since the tests were
    written.

