smartclockmon (0.6.6-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Show one receiver at a time.  The web view and the monitor both
    filter by receiver and offer a selector; a log holding two units no
    longer draws them as one trace.
  * A command a model does not have no longer voids the rest of the
    poll.  A Z3805A has no TFOM in its dialect, and that one gap left
    every later field on the tier unread and the snapshot unstamped.
  * Sixteen commands added to the Z3801 dialect -- temperature, oven
    current, EFC count, TFOM, date and time among them -- each confirmed
    against a Z3805A and against the firmware's own keyword table.
  * The monitor's journal is ordered by the receiver's own sequence.  A
    stamp is elapsed time since boot until the first GPS lock, so
    power-on entries sorted above what preceded them.

