smartclockmon (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * New: smartclock-exporter, Prometheus metrics served from the
    daemon's own readings, so a scrape costs the receiver nothing.  A
    reading the receiver declined is left out rather than exported as
    zero, and the age of each poll tier is exported so that a daemon
    which has stopped polling cannot pass for a steady oscillator.
  * The monitor's ASCII mode is gone: ratatui draws chart axes with
    box-drawing glyphs a caller cannot replace, so the fallback could
    never have been complete.
  * smartclock-cli --socket asks a running daemon instead of taking the
    serial port, so queries and diagnose work while logging continues.

